{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Because that Abraham listened to My voice.</b> This is the Binding (Akedah), and so it says (Genesis 22:18): 'עֵקֶב אֲשֶׁר שָׁמַעְתָּ בְּקֹלִי.'" "<b>And kept My charge.</b> This is circumcision, which he received immediately, as it is written (Genesis 17:10): 'זֹאת בְּרִיתִי אֲשֶׁר תִּשְׁמְרוּ' etc." "<b>My commandments.</b> This is circumcision on the eighth day, as it is written (Genesis 21:4): 'וַיָּמָל אַבְרָהָם אֶת יִצְחָק בְּנוֹ בֶּן שְׁמֹנַת יָמִים כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה אֹתוֹ אֱלֹהִים.'" "<b>My statutes.</b> That He would likewise command his seed after him to be circumcised. As it is written (Genesis 17:13): 'וְהָיְתָה בְרִיתִי בִּבְשַׂרְכֶם לִבְרִית עוֹלָם,' and it says (Psalms 105:10): 'וַיַּעֲמִידָהּ לְיַעֲקֹב לְחֹק' etc." "<b>And My Torah.</b> That I said to him: 'Go for yourself to the land that I will show you' (Genesis 12:1) — and a proof for the matter: 'אֲשְׂכִּילְךָ וְאוֹרְךָ בְּדֶרֶךְ זוּ תֵלֵךְ' (Psalms 32:8), and likewise 'יוֹרֶנִּי בְּדֶרֶךְ יִבְחָר' (Psalms 25:12), and so all 'Torah' is the language of instruction (hora'ah). And according to the plain sense, <b>My commandments, My statutes</b> are the seven commandments that the children of Noah were commanded."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:10.599789123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}